<p>The basic State Pension is one part of what people on the older system receive. Many of them also get Additional State Pension, which was based on their earnings. The new State Pension replaced both parts with a single amount. So the gap between {{ "bsp-full-weekly" | fig }} and {{ "nsp-full-weekly" | fig }} does not show that people on the older system receive less in total. The averages in <a href="#what-people-receive">What people actually receive</a> show this.</p>
